 "rationale": "Round 3 fitted better than the reference (CV 0.73 vs 0.91 cm-1), but its four extras are poorly constrained, so this round replaces them with one physically motivated term. Kept from round 3: the six signed F2 well vectors, which give F1+F2 and match the N+=0 F2-only pattern, plus the rotor axes and the nearest-well hop w[1,3]. New term: the Coriolis coupling -2B J.L projected on the wells. For a p-like F2 carrier, <v_i|L|v_j> = -i v_i x v_j. With v1 = (0,1,1)/sqrt2 and v3 = -(1,0,1)/sqrt2, v1 x v3 = (-1,-1,1)/2, which fixes the operator as i w[1,3] (Jz - Jx - Jy). This is the gz:gxy = 1:-1 ratio that the CH4+ fit found without being told (5.91, -5.74), so gz and gxy merge into one parameter, gL. Symmetry check by hand: sigma(x=y) sends v1 -> -v3 and v3 -> -v1, and sends J -> -(Jy,Jx,Jz), so Jz - Jx - Jy changes sign. The term therefore maps to its own Hermitian conjugate and is invariant. Dropped: sigmaJ, because its fitted values have opposite signs (CH4+ 1.34, CD4+ -1.73) and are large compared with sigma. Dropped: gopp, because CH4+ gives about 0 (-0.13) and CD4+ gives -1.48, which is implausible for opposite-well coupling when |sigma| is about 0.1 cm-1. Caveats: (1) CD4+ does not show the 1:-1 ratio (gz -0.11, gxy -0.59), but those shifts are only 0.05 and 0.28 prior sd, so they constrain it weakly. (2) The fitted CH4+ magnitude of about 5.8 cm-1 exceeds the Coriolis estimate of roughly 5*zeta*S cm-1, where S is the well overlap and is likely well below 1. The direction supports this mechanism, but the size is unexplained and gL may still be absorbing other effects. (3) Round 3 gave sigma opposite signs in the two isotopologues (CH4+ +3.93, CD4+ -0.106) with a CD4+ shift of only 0.003 prior sd, so sigma was not determined there. This model should be judged on whether sigma's sign and determination improve, even if CV rises somewhat with fewer parameters. This spec has not been compiled or fitted. The term's grammar and independence from the other terms are inferred from the round 3 compile.",
